  "body": "Problem as far as I can see (I am not familiar with matrix but currently reading the blog and the specs):\r\nbig events (e.g. files) get synced between instances and can cause a lot of traffic and space usage (maybe there are some filter mechanics I am not aware of).\r\nSo my proposal is:\r\nadd a lazy Placeholder event (I call it later transfer event) with an transfer reference for events with a bigger size than a treshold.\r\nThe transfer event can then be used to request a transfer of the big event. This can be deprioritized and slowly transferred or just denied in case of not enough space, no permission of the client, …\r\nIf the transfer is denied/failed it can be retried.\r\nIf it succeeds the big event is now replacing the transfer event and returned for the requesting clients.\r\n\r\nI am sorry for my imprecise language but I have no time to get into the matrix terminology.",
